variants/kits/ — the set library (D25)

Every Portage set Bentoo ships lives here, as kits/<category>/<name>. Layers
(base, flavor/<f>, ...) hold configuration and a selection -- the `sets:` list
in their recipe -- and no set content of their own.

Rules:
  - A set's file location does not decide who installs it. Only the sets a
    recipe declares are installed, plus every @ref they reach
    (shidashi.resolve.install_sets).
  - Categories are for people. Portage's set namespace is flat
    (/etc/portage/sets/<name>), so a name is unique across the whole library;
    tests/test_variants.py enforces it, and install_sets refuses a duplicate.
  - There is no same-name override between layers. A flavor tunes a set by
    declaring it, or by `exclude:`-ing atoms from it in its recipe.
  - The kits are the binhost's library, not only the images' contents. A line
    whose `#` is glued to an atom or @ref is built for the binhost and installed
    by NO image:
        #dev-lang/rust
        #@kde-apps        (the whole kit)
    A comment with a space (`# text`) is prose. To drop a package entirely,
    delete its line: commenting it out WITHOUT a space puts it in the binhost.
    shidashi drops the marked lines when it writes an image's sets
    (shidashi.resolve.kit_view) and `shidashi kits check` validates them.
    `exclude:` stays for per-image exceptions; excluding a catalog-only atom is
    an error. `shidashi world <image>` lists both, marked.
  - A stage's `include:` puts back, from that stage on, an atom an earlier
    stage excluded or a kit marks catalog-only. It becomes the stage's own set,
    @include-<stage>, installed by that stage's phase only: the kit stays
    filtered, so the shared fork points of earlier stages never get the atom.
    Including what nothing took out, or including and excluding the same atom,
    is an error. No kit may be named include-*.
  - This README is the only non-set file here; the index skips README and
    dotfiles.

Categories:
  core/      the universal core: @base and its leaves
  system/    console kits: @extra-system and its leaves
  graphics/  graphical infrastructure: gpu, fonts, desktop integration
  services/  system services: vpn, print, sandbox
  internet/  web, comms, p2p, remote
  media/     audio, video, imaging
  dev/       devel, containers
  office/    office suites
  virt/      virtualization
  groups/    the extra-* aggregators flavors choose from
  desktops/  one set per desktop flavor
